# Places where a mutant would tell nobody anything. One path to a line.
# See scratch/docs/07-MUTATION.md §5.4.
#
# This list is lingo's, not assay's. Nothing general belongs on it: the trace
# calls in lib/runtime/layout.ml read as logging in any other codebase and are
# not logging here, because law_layout part (g) counts the steps and dropping
# one goes red. A name earns its place here by a survivor proving it useless,
# not by looking unimportant.

# A formatter's arguments are computed for a reader and nothing reads them
# back. Everything inside the call goes with it.
Format.printf
Format.eprintf
Format.fprintf
Format.asprintf
Format.kasprintf
Format.sprintf
Printf.printf
Printf.eprintf
Printf.fprintf
Printf.sprintf
Printf.ksprintf
print_string
print_endline
print_newline
prerr_endline

# Raising. The message is for a reader, and the decision to raise is made by
# the test above it, which is mutated on its own.
failwith
invalid_arg
